From 9ddfb9e651d9420285dfeebc3e5f17d69d32bf1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:36:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] survivable processes: review fixes (daemon-safe tee,
 exact markers, shutdown sweep, Stop precedence, unit check)

- tee runs in a process substitution bash waits for at most ~1 s: a command leaving a daemon on
  its stdout (server &) returns when bash exits instead of hanging to its timeout.
- the log tail strips only the session's own PIPE/CWD markers (checkpointed shell_markers).
- with the key on, the gateway's shutdown kill_all spares persisted jobs it spawned (they were
  SIGKILLed by the sweep before the unit stop could spare them).
- a shutdown interrupt after a pending user Stop keeps the Stop reason on the tool thread too.
- usable() requires a systemd user unit, matching persisted_job_scope_argv's scope decision.
